-- title:
--   Greenberg–Wiles count for ad⁰ρ̄ at Taylor–Wiles level
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be an odd prime, $k$ a finite field that is an algebra over $\mathbb{F}_p$, and put $f=\dim_{\mathbb{F}_p}k$. Let $\bar\rho$ consist of a two-dimensional $k$-space $V$ together with a homomorphism $\bar\rho\colon\Gamma_{\mathbb Q}=\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)\to\mathrm{End}_k(V)$ that is trivial on the elements fixing some finite extension of $\mathbb Q$ inside $\overline{\mathbb Q}$. Assume: $\bar\rho$ is absolutely irreducible, i.e. the base change to $\overline{k}$ has no stable submodule other than $\bot$ and $\top$; the determinant is cyclotomic in the sense that $p=0$ in $k$ and, whenever $\sigma$ acts on the $p^n$-th roots of unity by $\mu\mapsto\mu^{a}$, $\det\bar\rho(\sigma)-a$ lies in the ideal generated by $p^n$ in $k$; and for every field $K$ over $k$ and every subgroup $G\le\Gamma_{\mathbb Q}$ of index $2$, every $K$-submodule of $K\otimes_k V$ stable under $G$ is $\bot$ or $\top$. Let $\rho_0$ be an $\mathbb F_p$-linear representation of $\Gamma_{\mathbb Q}$ on the trace-zero endomorphisms $\ker(\mathrm{tr}\colon\mathrm{End}_k V\to k)$ agreeing pointwise with the conjugation action `ρbar.adZeroRep`, and write $M=$ `Rep.of ρ₀`. Let $S,Q$ be finite sets of primes with $p\in S$, $S\cap Q=\emptyset$, with $\bar\rho$ unramified outside $S$ (trivial on the inertia image of every valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lying over $q\notin S$), and with every $q\in Q$ satisfying $q\equiv 1\pmod p$ and: for every valuation subring lying over $q$ and every $\varphi$ that is a Frobenius at $q$ for it (acting as $x\mapsto x^{q}$ on the residue field), the characteristic polynomial of $\bar\rho(\varphi)$ is $(X-\alpha)(X-\beta)$ with $\alpha\neq\beta$ in $k$. Then, with `continuousH1S (S ∪ Q)` denoting the submodule of $H^1(\Gamma_{\mathbb Q},-)$ which is the image of the level-$(S\cup Q)$ cocycles `levelCocyclesS₁ (S ∪ Q)` under the projection to $H^1$, and with the local maps being restriction along $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb Q}_q/\mathbb Q_q)\to\Gamma_{\mathbb Q}$ in degree $1$,
--   $$\dim_{\mathbb F_p}\Big(\mathrm{continuousH1S}(S\cup Q,M)\cap\bigcap_{q\in S}\ker\mathrm{res}_q\Big)+f+f\sum_{q\in S}\dim_k\big(\mathrm{ad}^0\bar\rho\big)^{\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb Q}_q/\mathbb Q_q)}\le f\,\#Q+\dim_{\mathbb F_p}\Big(\mathrm{continuousH1S}(S\cup Q,M^{*}(\chi_p))\cap\bigcap_{q\in Q}\ker\mathrm{res}_q\Big),$$
--   where $M^{*}(\chi_p)$ is the dual of $M$ twisted by the mod $p$ cyclotomic character `cycloChar p`.
--
--   This is the Galois-cohomological bookkeeping of the Taylor–Wiles method: the Greenberg–Wiles formula for $\mathrm{ad}^0\bar\rho$ with the conditions at $S$ left unspecified, after evaluating the global and archimedean invariant terms ($H^0(\mathbb Q,\mathrm{ad}^0\bar\rho)=0$ and $\dim_k H^0(\mathbb R,\mathrm{ad}^0\bar\rho)=1$) and bounding the local contribution at each auxiliary prime $q\in Q$. It feeds the selection of Taylor–Wiles primes in [`ResidualGaloisRep.exists_taylorWilesPrimes_finrank_span_dualNumberClasses_le_strictOrdinary`](thm.html#ResidualGaloisRep.exists_taylorWilesPrimes_finrank_span_dualNumberClasses_le_strictOrdinary).
